userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The four principal rays from an object's tip locate its image: for a concave mirror the reflected rays physically converge to a real, inverted image, while for a convex mirror they diverge and only their dashed backward extensions meet at a virtual, upright image behind the mirror.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): An image is simply where the rays from a point on the object meet — if they meet in real space the image is real and inverted (concave); if only their backward extensions meet, the image is virtual and upright behind the mirror (convex).
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
  "concept": "The four principal rays from an object's tip locate its image: for a concave mirror the reflected rays physically converge to a real, inverted image, while for a convex mirror they diverge and only their dashed backward extensions meet at a virtual, upright image behind the mirror.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Horizontal optical axis (thin gray line) spanning the panel",
    "Mirror drawn as a pale blue/white curved arc on the right, concave (bulging right) or convex (bulging left) depending on mode",
    "Mirror vertex V labeled where the arc crosses the axis",
    "Focal point F marked as a small red dot on the axis (in front of mirror for concave, behind for convex)",
    "Center of curvature C marked as a small black dot on the axis (in front for concave, behind for convex)",
    "Object: thick red upward arrow at far left, base P (blue dot) on the axis, tip Q labeled above; text label 'Object' to its left",
    "Image: red arrow at P' — short downward (inverted) arrow between C and F for concave; smaller upright arrow behind the mirror between V and F for convex; tip labeled Q'",
    "Curved leader arrow with text label 'Image' pointing to the image arrow tip",
